{"id":"hemeonc-anatomy","system":"Hematology & Oncology","subject":"Anatomy","pages":[412,415],"rounds":[{"t":"Hematopoiesis and neutrophils","q":[{"s":"Which stem cell gives rise to erythrocytes, platelets, granulocytes and monocytes?","o":["Neural crest cell","Monoblast","Lymphoid stem cell","Mesenchymal stem cell","Myeloid stem cell"],"e":["Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Monocyte precursor only.","Wrong. Gives B, T and NK cells.","Wrong. Not hematopoietic.","Correct."],"a":4,"p":"412","k":"Hematopoiesis"},{"s":"NK cells arise from which precursor?","o":["Megakaryoblast","Myeloblast","Myeloid stem cell","Lymphoid stem cell","Monoblast"],"e":["Wrong. Platelets.","Wrong. Granulocytes.","Wrong. Not correct.","Correct. With B and T cells.","Wrong. Not correct."],"a":3,"p":"412","k":"Hematopoiesis"},{"s":"Which cell is the direct precursor of platelets?","o":["Myeloblast","Megakaryocyte","Erythroblast","Lymphoblast","Monoblast"],"e":["Wrong. Granulocytes.","Correct. Platelets are cytoplasmic fragments of megakaryocytes.","Wrong. RBCs.","Wrong. Lymphocytes.","Wrong. Monocytes."],"a":1,"p":"412","k":"Hematopoiesis"},{"s":"Plasma cells differentiate from which blood cell?","o":["Basophil","B cell","T cell","NK cell","Monocyte"],"e":["Wrong. Not correct.","Correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Becomes a macrophage."],"a":1,"p":"412","k":"Hematopoiesis"},{"s":"The immediate circulating precursor of the mature erythrocyte is the:","o":["Reticulocyte","Megakaryoblast","Erythroblast","Band","Myeloblast"],"e":["Correct.","Wrong. Not correct.","Wrong. Remains in marrow.","Wrong. Neutrophil precursor.","Wrong. Not correct."],"a":0,"p":"412","k":"Hematopoiesis"},{"s":"Which enzyme is found in the specific granules of neutrophils?","o":["β-glucuronidase","Leukocyte alkaline phosphatase","Acid phosphatase","Myeloperoxidase","Major basic protein"],"e":["Wrong. Azurophilic granules.","Correct. Also collagenase, lysozyme and lactoferrin.","Wrong. Azurophilic granu